        {
          "ruleId": "CWE-862",
          "level": "error",
          "message": {
            "text": "MISSING TENANCY/AUTHORIZATION FILTER on nine dataset sub-resource routes: their SQL never constrains by project_id, so they operate on any row id globally. Confirmed: `datasets.delete(\"/:id\")` at line 111 runs `delete from dataset where id = ${id}` with NO project_id predicate; `datasets.get(\"/prompts/:id\")` line 149 `select * from dataset_prompt where id = ${id}`; `datasets.delete(\"/prompts/:id\")` line 166; `datasets.patch(\"/prompts/:id\")` line 176 `update dataset_prompt set messages = ${messages} where id = ${id}`; `datasets.get(\"/variations/:id\")` line 188; `datasets.delete(\"/variations/:id\")` line 202; `datasets.patch(\"/variations/:variationId\")` line 211; `datasets.post(\"/prompts\")` line 120 (datasetId taken from request body, unverified); `datasets.post(\"/variations\")` line 243 (promptId from body, unverified). The safe pattern IS present elsewhere in the same file/module (datasets.get(\"/\") line 13 and datasets.patch(\"/:id\") line 96 both use `project_id = ${projectId}`; datasets/utils.ts:6 `select * from dataset where id = ${datasetId} and project_id = ${projectId}`), which shows the control was intended and is simply absent on these nine. Because of the `/v1/datasets/.+` public-route regex these are reachable with NO credentials at all, giving unauthenticated cross-tenant read, modification and deletion of dataset/prompt/variation data.\n\nVerifier (CONFIRM): Re-derived independently from source. Nine dataset sub-resource handlers in packages/backend/src/api/v1/datasets/index.ts execute SQL keyed solely on a client-supplied row id with no project_id predicate and no ownership join: DELETE /:id (L114 `delete from dataset where id = ${id}` \u2014 the handler never even destructures projectId from ctx.state), GET/DELETE/PATCH /prompts/:id (L153, L169-170, L183), GET/DELETE/PATCH /variations/:id (L192, L205, L227-235), plus POST /prompts (L121-132, datasetId taken from request body unverified) and POST /variations (L244-261, promptId from body unverified). The control was clearly intended and is simply absent here: the same file uses `where project_id = ${projectId}` at L17 and `where id = ${id} and project_id = ${projectId}` at L105, and datasets/utils.ts:6 uses `where id = ${datasetId} and project_id = ${projectId}`. The DB schema proves the join is mandatory rather than optional: db/init.sql:419 gives `dataset` a project_id, but `dataset_prompt` (L430-436) and `dataset_prompt_variation` (L440-448) carry NO project_id column, so tenancy is only expressible by joining through dataset. Unauthenticated reach is confirmed end-to-end: auth/utils.ts:76 registers `new RegExp('/v1/datasets/.+')` in publicRoutes, and auth/utils.ts:90-96 short-circuits to `await next()` when `isPublicRoute && !bearerToken` with zero credential validation; authMiddleware is mounted globally at src/index.ts:34 ahead of `app.use(v1.routes())` at L41, with the datasets router mounted at api/v1/index.ts:39 under prefix /v1. All nine paths carry a segment after /v1/datasets/, so all match the regex. Net effect: an attacker with NO credentials can read, modify and delete any tenant's dataset, prompt and variation rows by id; `DELETE /v1/datasets/<id>` additionally cascades (ON DELETE CASCADE, init.sql:435/447) to destroy all child prompts and variations. I did NOT downgrade on the graph's reachable_from_entry=false because that flag is false for all 13 routes in this file including the demonstrably-live safe handlers at L13 and L96 \u2014 the documented arrow-function under-linking artifact \u2014 so I established reach from the source mount chain instead. Exploit-reference check was attempted but the Metasploit corpus is unindexed; it is advisory only and this is a first-party source defect with no versioned component to pin, so it does not affect the verdict. Corrected the analyst's end line from 243 to 264 (the final handler extends to 264)."
          },
